{"term":"lumber","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:95fb55e709f6a19c2b","definition":"Wood sawn into planks or otherwise prepared for sale or use, especially as a building material.","example":"Here they live by fishing on the most plentiful coasts in the world; there they fell trees, by the sides of large rivers, for masts and lumber […].","pos":"noun","synonyms":["timber","wood"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Canada, US, usually","register":"Canada, US, uncountable, usually","wordFamily":["bring the lumber","dimensional lumber","dimension lumber","lumberdom","lumberer","lumberjack","lumber jacket","lumber-jacketed","lumberless","lumberly","lumberman","lumbermill","lumber pie","lumberroom","lumber room","lumbersome","Lumberton","Lumberville","lumberwood","lumbery","lumberyard","lumber yard"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lumber#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:67015974d4aa016000","definition":"Old furniture or other items that take up room, or are stored away.","example":"On the ſecond day of my impriſonment, I was viſited by the duke of L⁠—⁠—, a friend of my lord, who found me ſitting upon a trunk, in a poor little dining-room filled with lumber, and lighted with two bits of tallow-candle, which had been left over night.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["timber","wood"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic, usually","register":"archaic, uncountable, usually","wordFamily":["bring the lumber","dimensional lumber","dimension lumber","lumberdom","lumberer","lumberjack","lumber jacket","lumber-jacketed","lumberless","lumberly","lumberman","lumbermill","lumber pie","lumberroom","lumber room","lumbersome","Lumberton","Lumberville","lumberwood","lumbery","lumberyard","lumber yard"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lumber#English","license":"CC-